<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Soothe</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Ranger (guild level 3, up to 75%), Druid (guild level 13, up to 75%)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>soothe &lt;monster&gt;
</pre>
<p>Calms an aggressive monster towards you. Once soothed, it warms to you and 
won't attack you again, though it stays as aggressive as ever to everyone 
else; it remembers you until it dies.
</p><p>Only some aggressive monsters can be soothed; with the others, you sense 
that they are immune. The monster must be awake and not fighting, and you 
can't soothe while you are fighting yourself. Your skill and your charisma 
against the monster's decide it: if you fail, nothing happens, but if you 
fail badly, you provoke it into attacking you.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Ranger</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Druid</a>
</pre>




</div>